(LICENSES/CSSL-v1.0.txt, SPDX LicenseRef-CSSL-1.0). IntEdge changes (2026-10-25):
  - b2xx mode rendered: the USE_B2XX environment entry was indented one level too deep (a YAML parse error) and
    carried a boolean value (refused by the Kubernetes API);
  - the gnb container declared env: twice; the second (TZ, USE_ADDITIONAL_OPTIONS) replaced the first, so
    OAI_GDBSTACKS and the radio's USE_* variable never reached it: one env block now;
  - radio.firmware: "baked" (the image carries the USRP firmware) or "download" (upstream behaviour: fetched from
    the internet at every start);
  - radio.usbAccess: the b2xx container is privileged so it can open the B210 again after it reconnects;
  - nfimage.digest; the init containers' images pinned by digest (images.*); imagePullSecrets empty by default;
  - the ConfigMap declared config.yaml twice (an empty one, then AsConfig's): once now;
  - config.yaml: sdr_addrs "type=b200" instead of a placeholder serial.

